    "Interpenetration commonly occurs in pillar-layered frameworks, especially with large carboxylates, and it reduces accessible void by promoting close packing.",
    "Choosing 5-amino-1H-tetrazole as the grid-forming ligand was proposed to suppress harmful interpenetration and maximize accessible space.",
